+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "0500af506053",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### 3. Prepare the inputs and initialize the model\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For each station the processor sorts by date, keeps rows with missing labels, and splits at missing daily dates. Contiguous series of the same length T are batched together; no convolution crosses a station or date gap. Each group supplies `[N, T, 8]` temporal inputs, `[N, 7]` static inputs and `[N, T]` targets. Static columns must stay constant within a station. The builder also supplies the training source/target scaler statistics. The model sums corrected sources in physical units; `threshold: null` gives each source a physical lower bound of zero."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "id": "f268817a02f7",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "prepared = prepare_pm25(train_df, val_df, test_df, model_name=cfg[\"model\"][\"name\"])\n",
+    "model = build_model(cfg[\"model\"][\"name\"], cfg[\"model\"][\"kwargs\"], prepared)\n",
+    "first_group = next(iter(prepared.train.tensors.values()))\n",
+    "print(\"First training group's input(s) and targets:\", [tuple(x.shape) for x in first_group])\n",
